codex
A protocol ambiguity surfaced while detailing resource limits: v1 says association count, queued bytes, datagram size, and idle timeout are negotiated, but the specified hello only carries features and `maxFrame`, and no limits message exists. I’m adding an explicit blocking decision task rather than inventing an incompatible wire extension; the chosen resolution will gate schema, negotiation, vectors, and UDP limit enforcement.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'create(type=task, parent=STORY-260715-18ncz1, name=resolve-protocol-v1-resource-limit-exchange, description=\"Resolve the mismatch between the v1 wire layout and the requirement to negotiate association, queue, datagram, and idle limits, selecting a compatibility-safe implementable contract before schema and codec work freezes.\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy
