ormalized candidates\\nSSH --> Coordinator : exact platform tuple\\nCoordinator -> Manifest : select one trusted asset\\nCoordinator -> SSH : create private random temporary path\\nCoordinator -> SSH : stream exact binary bytes with bounded writes\\nCoordinator -> SSH : verify size and SHA-256\\nalt approved hash utility exists\\n  SSH -> Shell : fixed sha256sum or shasum operation\\n  Shell --> SSH : one strict digest record\\nelse no approved hash utility\\n  SSH -> Shell : bounded binary readback\\n  Shell --> SSH : exact file bytes\\n  SSH --> Coordinator : client computes SHA-256\\nend\\nCoordinator -> SSH : chmod 0700 and atomic versioned rename\\nCoordinator -> SSH : exec exact verified path --stdio --protocol 1\\nSSH -> Relay : launch with separate stdin, stdout, stderr\\nRelay --> Coordinator : protocol hello plus build identity and limits\\nalt all evidence matches\\n  Coordinator -> Capability : publish relay-ready evidence\\nelse any mismatch or timeout\\n  Coordinator -> SSH : close channel and clean owned temporary state\\n  Coordinator -> Capability : publish finite degraded reason\\nend\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"Planning sequence diagram for authenticated upload, verification, atomic install, and handshake\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-1loqwb, name=TASK-260715-1loqwb_udp-data-path.puml, content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\ntitle Full-mode UDP and DNS data path\\n\\nparticipant \\\"HEV UDP-in-TCP\\\" as HEV\\nparticipant \\\"Client association registry\\\" as Registry\\nparticipant \\\"SSH relay frame pump\\\" as Pump\\nparticipant \\\"relux-relay association registry\\\" as Relay\\nparticipant \\\"Exit-host UDP socket\\\" as Socket\\nparticipant \\\"Destination or resolver\\\" as Dest\\n\\nHEV -> Registry : validated IPv4, IPv6, or domain datagram\\nRegistry -> Registry : allocate or reuse active generation association ID\\nRegistry -> Pump : UDP_DATAGRAM within effective limits\\nalt queue has capacity\\n  Pump -> Relay : framed bytes over SSH exec stdio\\n  Relay -> Socket : bounded association socket send\\n  Socket -> Dest : UDP datagram from user host\\n  Dest --> Socket : UDP response\\n  Socket --> Relay : source endpoint plus bytes\\n  Relay --> Pump : UDP_DATAGRAM response\\n  Pump --> Registry : association-scoped response\\n  Registry --> HEV : HEV frame with observed source endpoint\\nelse queue or resource limit reached\\n  Pump --> Registry : typed drop or bounded error\\n  Registry --> HEV : documented association-visible outcome\\nend\\n\\ngroup DNS priority without protocol privilege\\n  HEV -> Registry : tunnel-owned DNS query\\n  Registry -> Pump : priority class within fixed ceilings\\n  note right of Pump\\n  Control remains highest priority.\\n  DNS cannot bypass byte, time,\\n  association, or retry ceilings.\\n  end note\\nend\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"Planning sequence diagram for HEV datagrams, relay associations, DNS priority, and responses\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-30lv40, name=TASK-260715-30lv40_capability-state-plan.puml, content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\ntitle M2 capability state and relay-only recovery\\n\\n[*] --> Connecting\\nConnecting --> ConnectedFull : base TCP plus safe DNS plus validated relay\\nConnecting --> ConnectedDegraded : base TCP plus safe DNS, relay unavailable\\nConnecting --> Failed : mandatory TCP or safe DNS unavailable\\n\\nConnectedFull --> ConnectedDegraded : bootstrap, framing, health, process, or relay-lane failure\\nConnectedFull --> Failed : mandatory base path or safe DNS failure\\nConnectedDegraded --> RelayReprobe : recoverable relay reason and healthy base SSH\\nRelayReprobe --> ConnectedFull : fresh asset, identity, handshake, features, limits, health\\nRelayReprobe --> ConnectedDegraded : bounded attempt fails, retry remains eligible\\nRelayReprobe --> Failed : mandatory base path or safe DNS fails\\nConnectedDegraded --> Failed : safe DNS or TCP becomes unusable\\n\\nConnecting --> Stopping : provider stop\\nConnectedFull --> Stopping : provider stop\\nConnectedDegraded --> Stopping : provider stop\\nRelayReprobe --> Stopping : provider stop\\nFailed --> Stopping : provider stop\\nStopping --> [*]\\n\\nnote right of ConnectedFull\\nTCP: usable\\nSafe DNS: usable\\nGeneral UDP: relay only\\nend note\\n\\nnote right of ConnectedDegraded\\nTCP: usable\\nSafe DNS: tunneled fallback only\\nGeneral UDP: explicitly rejected\\nNo physical fallback\\nend note\\n\\nnote bottom of RelayReprobe\\nM2 owns relay-only reprobe on the healthy authenticated base transport.\\nM3 owns path, host, route, lane-pool, sleep, NAT64, and captive reconnect.\\nend note\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"Planning state diagram for full, degraded, failed, and relay-only restoration\"); add_resource(EPIC-260715-2lz67t, name=EPIC-260715-2lz67t_dependency-plan.dot, content=\"digraph M2 {\\n  rankdir=LR;\\n  graph [label=\\\"EPIC-260715-2lz67t M2 dependency plan\\\", labelloc=t, fontsize=18];\\n  node [shape=box, style=\\\"rounded,filled\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#E8F1FB\\\"];\\n\\n  Foundation [label=\\\"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm\\\\nGate A0, target graph, HEV and SSH decisions\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#F6E8C3\\\"];\\n  M1 [label=\\\"EPIC-260715-3810we\\\\nAuthenticated SSH, TCP, tunnel DNS, runtime and physical baselines\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#F6E8C3\\\"];\\n\\n  Protocol [label=\\\"STORY-260715-18ncz1\\\\nRelay protocol v1 and conformance\\\"];\\n  Build [label=\\\"STORY-260715-3pv7qc\\\\nPortable assets and manifest\\\"];\\n  Bootstrap [label=\\\"STORY-260715-2etfkl\\\\nSecure bootstrap and relay session\\\"];\\n  UDP [label=\\\"STORY-260715-1nsw9p\\\\nBounded UDP and DNS over relay\\\"];\\n  Capability [label=\\\"STORY-260715-2ungml\\\\nLeak-safe degraded capability\\\"];\\n\\n  Foundation -> Protocol [label=\\\"approved target and relay-toolchain boundary\\\"];\\n  M1 -> Bootstrap [label=\\\"authenticated bidirectional SSH exec\\\"];\\n  M1 -> UDP [label=\\\"HEV UDP mode, tunnel DNS and physical baseline\\\