eezing the M2 state contract. The extension remains live-state authority, system session state remains distinct, and M2 must extend rather than replace the M1 coordinator and message ownership rules.\", type=precondition, description=\"M1 runtime ownership prerequisite for capability states\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-2zmw58, name=TASK-260715-2zmw58_m1-resolver-decision.md, content=\"# Required resolver decision\\n\\nConsume the accepted outcome from TASK-260715-1tnjlu. This task may map that decision into M2 degraded behavior, but it must not select another resolver, vendor, transport default, or profile schema implicitly. If the M1 decision is not accepted, preserve the exact unresolved choice.\", type=precondition, description=\"Approved M1 resolver decision prerequisite for degraded DNS\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-3edgwz, name=TASK-260715-3edgwz_m1-snapshot-handoff.md, content=\"# Required M1 snapshot handoff\\n\\nConsume accepted outcomes from:\\n\\n- TASK-260715-lovbdz — versioned runtime configuration and message models\\n- TASK-260715-1i49fm — privacy-safe runtime diagnostics snapshots\\n\\nExtend these schemas compatibly for relay build, features, limits, mode, and finite reasons. Do not create a second live-state authority or expose remote-controlled diagnostic text.\", type=precondition, description=\"M1 versioned model and diagnostics prerequisites for M2 snapshots\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-3260rm, name=TASK-260715-3260rm_m1-safe-dns-handoff.md, content=\"# Required M1 safe-DNS handoff\\n\\nConsume accepted outcomes from:\\n\\n- TASK-260715-1tnjlu — exit resolver decision\\n- TASK-260715-1e0x1u — tunnel-owned DNS listener\\n- TASK-260715-5o6jqg — SSH DNS-over-TCP upstream\\n- TASK-260715-2hawz9 — bounded cache and fallback semantics\\n\\nIntegrate these components for degraded readiness and failure. Do not introduce a physical resolver path.\", type=precondition, description=\"M1 safe-DNS component prerequisites for degraded integration\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-2y78ah, name=TASK-260715-2y78ah_m1-harness-handoff.md, content=\"# Required M1 harness handoff\\n\\nConsume the accepted outcome from TASK-260715-336ljl. Reuse its controlled TCP and DNS fixtures, route-order instrumentation, external-IP observations, physical resolver sentinel, counters, revision capture, and cleanup baseline, then add relay failure, UDP rejection, restoration, and physical UDP sentinel rows.\", type=precondition, description=\"M1 composed routing and DNS harness prerequisite\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-3nkhry, name=TASK-260715-3nkhry_m1-iphone-baseline.md, content=\"# Required physical iPhone baseline\\n\\nConsume accepted evidence from TASK-260715-2qr5aj and the M2 UDP evidence from TASK-260715-2kfa02 before full, degraded, failed, and restoration acceptance. Preserve the same device, capture, redaction, revision, routing, DNS, and cleanup evidence contract.\", type=precondition, description=\"Physical iPhone M1 acceptance prerequisite for capability validation\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-10phgg, name=TASK-260715-10phgg_m1-macos-baseline.md, content=\"# Required physical Mac baseline\\n\\nConsume accepted evidence from TASK-260715-2wqffe and the M2 UDP evidence from TASK-260715-2m7lwo before full, degraded, failed, and restoration acceptance. Preserve the same device, capture, redaction, revision, routing, DNS, and cleanup evidence contract.\", type=precondition, description=\"Physical Mac M1 acceptance prerequisite for capability validation\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy
